      "writtenOn": "2026-08-10T08:56:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "DBus specification does not allow \".\" in the element name of the DBus object path\nBelow are the valid Dbus object path rules\n```\nThe path may be of any length.\nThe path must begin with an ASCII \u0027/\u0027 (integer 47) character, and must consist of elements separated by slash characters.\nEach element must only contain the ASCII characters \"[A-Z][a-z][0-9]_\"\nNo element may be the empty string.\nMultiple \u0027/\u0027 characters cannot occur in sequence.\nA trailing \u0027/\u0027 character is not allowed unless the path is the root path (a single \u0027/\u0027 character).\n```\n\nSo the dotted Ip address can not be used in the Dbus object path.",
